# .graphifyignore — controls what graphify walks when building the knowledge graph.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
# graphify prefers .graphifyignore over .gitignore PER DIRECTORY (it reads one or
# the other, never both). So this file must MIRROR .gitignore to avoid regressing
# the excludes graphify already relied on, PLUS add ML-data/capture dumps that are
# committed to git on purpose (data/captures/ has ~3k tracked files) but are pure
# noise for a CODE knowledge graph.
#
# If you change .gitignore, mirror the relevant lines here too.
# Build/dep dirs (target, node_modules, dist, build, .venv, __pycache__, ...) are
# ALWAYS skipped by graphify internally — no need to list them.

